# Intent: Owner request (2026-11-17), part 2 of 2: the screens, drawn by the unit's own LVGL code (maipai_apps.cc) and wired to the unit (maipai_pages_unit.cc). The sheet's Apps tile opens the Apps wall (two pages of big tiles with the dots under them; a swipe left or right changes page); each app opens: Timers and Alarms are screens of their own, Clock, Quick actions, Pictures and Dashboard open the swipe page of that name, Dance dances (refused with a plain line in quiet or mute), Lock locks at once with the passcode lock (patches LK02 and LK03) or, with no code set, shows the hint to set a code on the settings page. The sheet's Games tile opens the same wall for the games the unit holds (read from the games table, so it follows whatever games exist). Timers: quick presets of 1, 5, 10 and 15 minutes, the running timers with the time left and a 44 px Cancel each (the list scrolls past three), and a Countdown button that is reserved and off for the later full screen countdown (MAC_COUNTDOWN_READY 0, host hook countdown_open). Alarms: the set alarms (time and label) with a Cancel each and Add alarm: a time picker with hour and minute steppers (a long press repeats), AM or PM on a 12 hour clock and Save, using the timer core's own add and cancel (no new storage format). Settings (the gear): a tab column General, Network, Faces, Info always on the left and a scrolling list on the right with a scroll indicator, a Done target, and a swipe down that begins on the top strip closes. General: volume and brightness sliders (20 px of empty room under each knob and taps ignored for 300 ms after a slider is let go, as patch QS01), Night dim and Status icons switches, the auto lock choice and Lock now (the lock hooks), the language (read only) and More settings (time zone and network test). Network: the Wi-Fi page link, the network name, the signal, the private network state and the hub address. Faces: the face style picker with a live preview (and the picture faces while a picture pack is held). Info: the release tag, the image state, the slot, the memory line and the host name; ten taps on the firmware line list the full details, as the version screen did. One overlay screen at a time (maipai_screens.h), nothing exists until a view opens (the 250 ms timer, the objects and one state record are made then and freed on close; at rest only pointers and three atomics, under 100 bytes of internal RAM). The wake word, speech, a ring, a game or half a minute (a minute in Settings) without a touch returns to the face.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_apps.h, maipai_apps.cc (ours, new), maipai_pages.h, maipai_pages.cc, maipai_pages_unit.cc (ours, P12, P13, UI05)
# Check after a flash: Swipe up, tap the Apps tile: the wall shows Timers, Alarms, Clock and Quick actions with two dots under the tiles; swipe left: Dashboard, Dance and Lock. Tap Timers, tap 5 and see a running timer with Cancel; swipe down from the top strip: the face returns. Tap Lock with no code set: the hint shows. Open Games from the sheet: the games wall. Tap the gear: the tabs on the left; drag the volume slider, change a tab, scroll the list, tap Done.
# Kconfig: CONFIG_MAIPAI_PAGES

diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/maipai_apps.h b/firmware/main/hal/maipai_apps.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/firmware/main/hal/maipai_apps.h
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+/*
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+ *
+ * The Apps wall, the Timers and Alarms apps and the tabbed Settings screen, drawing and wiring (patch UI16). Logic and layout:
+ * maipai_apps_core.h. Everything it reads or does goes through MaipaiPagesHost (maipai_pages.h), so the same code runs on the unit
+ * and in the host renderer (scripts/fw-face-render/apps_render.cc). Nothing exists until a view is opened (no timer, no objects, one
+ * state record of about 600 bytes in the heap); closing it frees all of it. One overlay screen at a time (maipai_screens.h).
+ */
+#pragma once
+#include <sdkconfig.h>
+
+#if CONFIG_MAIPAI_PAGES || defined(MAIPAI_HOST_RENDER)
+#include <lvgl.h>
+#include "maipai_pages.h"
+
+enum { MAV_APPS = 0, MAV_GAMES, MAV_TIMERS, MAV_ALARMS, MAV_SETTINGS, MAV_COUNT };
+
+// Hooks the screens up (called by maipai_pages_attach). Call with the LVGL lock held. Creates nothing.
+void maipai_apps_attach(MaipaiPagesHost* host, lv_color_t (*fg)());
+// Opens a view (MAV_*), closing whatever other overlay screen is up. LVGL lock held. False when locked, not attached or out of memory.
+bool maipai_apps_show(int view);
+// True while any of these screens is on the glass (the Settings screen included). Safe from any task.
+bool maipai_apps_open();
+// True while the Settings screen is the one up. Safe from any task.
+bool maipai_apps_settings_open();
+// An outside event (MGS_EV_*), from any task: the screen goes back to the face at the next tick. Does nothing while nothing is open.
+void maipai_apps_event(int ev);
+// Runs the 250 ms work now (the host renderer calls this instead of waiting for the timer).
+void maipai_apps_step();
+// Closes and frees everything. LVGL lock held.
+void maipai_apps_close();
+#else
+inline bool maipai_apps_open() { return false; }
+inline bool maipai_apps_settings_open() { return false; }
+inline void maipai_apps_event(int) {}
+inline void maipai_apps_close() {}
+#endif
diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/maipai_apps.cc b/firmware/main/hal/maipai_apps.cc
